    },
    {
      "path": "DavisKahan/Experimental/FiniteDimensional/Sharpness.lean",
      "reason": "The one-sided sinTwoAngleOperator has one nonzero singular value per principal plane, while the historical symmetric perturbation has two; arbitrary UI-norm equality is false. The retained operator-norm theorem is rank-insensitive and correct.",
