      "replacement": "sinTwoTheta_model_operatorNorm_equality"
    },
    {
      "correction": "Replace mixed ambient/subtype graph statements by the canonical rectangular trial-coordinate tangent perturbation theorem.",
      "date": "2026-07-21",
      "path": "DavisKahan/Experimental/FiniteDimensional/TanTheta/GraphOperator.lean"
    },
    {
      "correction": "Retire the false arbitrary-UI and contour-mixed family; retain the canonical finite coordinate definition and production bounded complex operator-norm theory.",
      "date": "2026-07-21",
      "path": "DavisKahan/Experimental/FiniteDimensional/DoubleAngle/TanTheta.lean"
    },
    "Finite direct rotation uses the global polar cosine |P_V P_U + P_Vperp P_Uperp|; the one-sided |P_V P_U| cannot appear in a full-space trigonometric identity.",
    "Davis--Kahan Proposition 4.4 is retained only over real inner-product spaces; the paper gives a complex counterexample.",
    "The direct-rotation uniqueness endpoint is polar-factor uniqueness for a unitary-positive factorization, replacing the fictional principal-plane square-root proof.",
    {
      "correction": "Replace the nonexistent Spectra.SpectralTheory.SpectralTheorem import by the actual vendored PVM and calculus modules, and place the genuine bounded complex spectral-projection core at the dependency root.",
      "date": "2026-07-21",
      "declarations": [
        "boundedSelfAdjointSpectralPVM",
        "boundedSelfAdjointSpectralProjection",
        "boundedSelfAdjointSpectralSubspace"
      ],
